---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import videos from "../../../data/feat-video-research.json";
import "../../styles/feats.css";
---

<Layout
  title="Feat point-farming plan"
  description="Plan DCUO feat sessions around preparation, nearby objectives, instance conditions and verified video chapters."
>
  <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/feats/">Feats</a>
    <span>/</span>
    <span>Point-farming plan</span>
  </nav>
  <h1>Build points with fewer wasted runs</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Start with unearned objectives you can finish now, group nearby tasks, then
    prepare coordinated instance attempts.
  </p>
  <p>
    This order is an editorial plan based on documented requirements. It is not
    a measured points-per-minute ranking. Your unlocked content, character,
    completed feats, currency and group change the best route.
  </p>
  <ol class="farming-sequence">
    <li>
      <h2>Check your character before picking targets</h2>
      <p>
        Open the in-game Feats menu and remove completed objectives from your
        list. Check faction, movement mode, level or combat rating, content
        access and event availability. Keep reward stars separate from our
        estimated difficulty bars.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/feats/?sort=priority&amp;quick=1">
          Find higher-reward quick objectives
        </a>
        . The quick queue excludes explicit item preparation, counters,
        progression and group conditions; it is a shortlist to inspect, not a
        guarantee of a short completion time.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h2>Finish a local sweep before travelling</h2>
      <p>
        Combine exploration checkpoints and other nearby objectives with
        missions you already need. Open the linked map and objective list before
        leaving. Add candidates to your session checklist, finish the local
        area, then travel to the next group.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/feats/?group=Exploration%20Feats&amp;sort=priority">
          Exploration objectives
        </a>{" "}
        ·{" "}
        <a href="/feats/?group=Races%20Feats&amp;sort=priority">
          Race objectives
        </a>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h2>Make a shopping list instead of buying blindly</h2>
      <p>
        Check partially completed style sets first. Separate items you can
        afford now from Source Mark, event-currency, collection, crafting and
        random-drop goals. Record missing pieces and exact costs in game; keep
        expensive or unavailable sets out of a quick-objective session.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/feats/?q=styles&amp;sort=points">
          Find style-set rewards and source lists
        </a>
        . Use the vendor-circuit video below for a preparation method, then
        confirm the current vendor inventory and currency yourself.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h2>Read every instance condition before queuing</h2>
      <p>
        Group feats by the actual mission or instance in your session checklist.
        Pick the required Normal, Elite or Elite Plus variant and agree who
        handles each mechanic. Compare timing, optional-enemy and no-knockout
        conditions before the first pull.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some objectives conflict, such as defeating an optional target versus
        keeping it alive. Plan separate attempts when necessary. Related guides
        and videos provide context; an instance video does not prove that every
        feat is demonstrated.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h2>Build counters while doing other useful content</h2>
      <p>
        Track repeat-completion, bounty, salvage and collection counters
        alongside your chosen sessions. Check progress after the attempt. Read
        all prerequisite feats before chasing a meta-feat reward; do not count
        the same faction alternative or archived version twice.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h2>Confirm the award and adjust the next session</h2>
      <p>
        Verify the feat popup or menu completion before checking an objective
        off your personal list. Every 100 feat points gives one skill point. The
        session total shows potential points from selected objectives, rather
        than points already earned or a prediction of your exact skill-point
        gain.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/feats/?sort=priority">Build your session checklist</a>
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <section>
    <h2>Timestamped preparation walkthrough</h2>
    {videos.records.map((v) => (
      <article>
        <h3>
          <a href={v.url}>{v.title}</a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          {v.evidence} Checked {videos.checked}. Chapters were checked against
          English automatic captions; the gameplay was not independently
          retested.
        </p>
        <iframe
          class="farming-video"
          src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/we9yLQauGSA?start=13"
          title={v.title}
          loading="lazy"
          allow="encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; fullscreen"
          allowfullscreen
          referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
        ></iframe>
        <ol>
          {v.chapters.map((c) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`${v.url}&t=${c.startSeconds}s`}>
                {Math.floor(c.startSeconds / 60)}:
                {String(c.startSeconds % 60).padStart(2, "0")} - {c.title}
              </a>
              <p>{c.instruction}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </article>
    ))}
  </section>
  <p>
    <a href="/wiki/Feats/">Feat-point and skill-point reference</a> ·{" "}
    <a href="/guides/">Mission guide library</a> ·{" "}
    <a href="/releases/">Episodes and chapters</a>
  </p>
</Layout>
